+## 9. Spec-replay probe (item "spec-replay")
+
+Setup — `bench/spec_replay.py OUTDIR LABEL SAMPLING [extra server args...]`:
+
+- OUTDIR = `bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay/`. Server cmd is the
+  production entry (`serving/llama-swap.bonsai-2-27b.yaml`) with `${PORT}` ->
+  8089 and `LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1` (exact prod flags: -np 2, --kv-unified,
+  --mmproj, --no-mmproj-offload, q4_0 K/V, --jinja). Fresh server per phase
+  (the n-gram pool persists across requests, so reusing it would inflate
+  acceptance). max_tokens = max(recorded predicted_n, 768 agent / 1024 mem),
+  identical in every arm. Slots pinned: agent 0, mem 1. Non-streaming.
+- Phases: single-agent (agent fg slot 0), single-mem (mem fg slot 1),
+  dual-agent (agent fg slot 0, mem loop bg slot 1), dual-mem (mem fg slot 1,
+  agent loop bg slot 0).
+
+Configs tested in this item:
+
+| Label | Flags | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| off | (none) | live baseline arm |
+| A | `--spec-type ngram-mod` | exact repeat of the documented `docs/engine-review.md` experiment (defaults: n-match 24, n-min 48, n-max 64) |
+| B | `--spec-type ngram-cache` | different ngram mechanism, chosen from `spec_flags.txt`: hash-based cached n-gram lookup rather than the fixed-window matching of ngram-mod, with no per-variant tuning flags. This is the "another ngram type" option from the item; it isolates mechanism change from threshold change (a second ngram-mod run with a different draft size would only test the same mechanism at a different parameter) |
+
+Script fixes applied for the spec runs (advisor review of the off/greedy run):
+
+- `timings.draft_n`/`draft_n_accepted` default to `0` when absent — the
+  fork only emits them when `n_draft_tokens > 0` (`tools/server/server-common.cpp`
+  82-85) — so every fg row in A/B carries integer fields.
+- The `--mmproj`/`--no-mmproj-offload` fallback re-run fires only on status
+  `refused` (log contains `unsupported batch.has_embd` / `not supported by
+  this context` / spec-disabled lines); any other failure (OOM, health timeout)
+  is noted and exits non-zero, not mislabelled as an mmproj refusal. On a
+  refusal it also auto-runs `off-{sampling}` without mmproj so the -nommproj
+  arms have a fair no-spec baseline in the same world.
+- Aborts before starting a server if `:8089/health` already answers (stale
+  server from a crashed run).
+
+Off/greedy baseline (2026-10-12, exit 0, 771 s total; `off-greedy/requests.jsonl`
+  committed, 151 rows, 0 errors):
+
+| Phase | fg | bg | median pps | weighted pps (all fg) | length rows | prompt_n / cache_n (median) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| single-agent | 30 | 0 | 55.7 | 56.2 | 1 | 1040.5 / 3166 |
+| single-mem | 12 | 0 | 48.9 | 55.6 | 0 | 533.5 / 8198 |
+| dual-agent | 30 | 60 mem | 30.7 | 26.3 | 0 | 1040.5 / 3166 |
+| dual-mem | 12 | 7 agent | 31.6 | 25.0 | 0 | 533.5 / 8198 |
+
+- The single length-capped row is `inventory-baseline-r1/2/8` (max_tokens =
+  recorded predicted_n = 1323; the greedy/temperature-0 path looped until the
+  cap). Per the advisor's note for item 4, report speedups with and without
+  capped/looping outputs, since greedy looping inflates n-gram gains.
+- VRAM 9507/10240 MiB after the first request in all four phases.
+- Live-entry reference (2026-10-11 baseline): 61.9 tok/s single stream,
+  43.8/44.8 tok/s both slots busy — the off numbers above are lower for
+  this traffic mix (many short tool-call turns, long mem prompts) and are the
+  apples-to-apples baseline for A/B on this probe.
+
+Next: A/greedy, then B/greedy, then prod for off and the better dual-agent
+A/B config.
+
